mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Backend API — Dual-Token Economy\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis canister implements a personal dual-token economy. Users sign in with Internet Identity, perform validated work to earn Me-Coins, stake Me-Coins to receive We-Coins governance power, and vote on governance proposals by spending 1 We-Coin per vote. It also exposes its persisted data through the OQL query layer and serves this API documentation.\n\n## Identity & Authentication\n\nSign-in uses Internet Identity (SSO). The frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin, for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`. Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n\nRegistration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend. A principal that never did so is unregistered even when it belongs to the app's owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered.\n\n### Registration prerequisite\n\nBefore any role-guarded call (guarded queries included), a direct API caller must register by calling `_initialize_access_control` once as a signed-in caller. The first caller to register becomes `#admin`; every subsequent caller becomes `#user`. Anonymous callers are ignored by registration.\n\nAn unregistered non-anonymous caller on a guarded endpoint traps with `User is not registered`. An anonymous caller is treated as `#guest` and is never trapped by the role lookup.\n\n## Roles\n\n- `#admin` — the first registered caller.\n- `#user` — every subsequent registered caller.\n- `#guest` — anonymous callers.\n\n## Public Methods\n\n### Authorization\n\n- `_internet_identity_sign_in_start() : async Blob` — shared. Issues a sign-in challenge. No caller check.\n- `_internet_identity_sign_in_finish() : async Result<(), Error>` — shared. Registers the caller (first becomes admin) and verifies the identity attributes.\n- `_initialize_access_control() : async ()` — shared. Registers the caller (first becomes admin). Call once before any role-guarded call.\n- `getCallerUserRole() : async UserRole` — query. Returns `#guest` for anonymous callers; the caller's role otherwise. Traps `User is not registered` for unregistered non-anonymous callers.\n- `assignCallerUserRole(user, role) : async ()` — shared. Admin-only. Traps `Unauthorized: Only admins can assign user roles` for non-admins.\n- `isCallerAdmin() : async Bool` — query. Traps `User is not registered` for unregistered non-anonymous callers.\n\n### Profile\n\n- `getMyProfile() : async ?User` — query. Requires a registered caller (traps `User is not registered` otherwise). Returns the caller's economy state (`meCoins`, `weCoins`, `stakedMeCoins`) or `null` if none exists yet.\n\n### Work & Earning Me-Coins\n\n- `performWork(title, description) : async WorkEntry` — shared. Requires a registered caller. Traps `Description must be at least 20 characters` when `description` is shorter than 20 characters. Mints 10 Me-Coins into the caller's balance and records a `#workEarned` activity event.\n- `getWorkHistory() : async [WorkEntry]` — query. Requires a registered caller. Returns all work entries.\n\n### Staking\n\n- `stakeForWeCoins(amount) : async ()` — shared. Requires a registered caller. Traps `Cannot stake more Me-Coins than balance` when `amount` exceeds the caller's Me-Coins. Converts Me-Coins to We-Coins and records a `#staked` activity event.\n- `unstakeWeCoins(amount) : async ()` — shared. Requires a registered caller. Traps `Cannot unstake more We-Coins than held` when `amount` exceeds the caller's We-Coins or staked Me-Coins. Converts We-Coins back to Me-Coins and records a `#unstaked` activity event.\n- `getStakingInfo() : async StakingInfo` — query. Requires a registered caller. Returns the caller's `stakedMeCoins`, `weCoins`, and `meCoins`.\n\n### Proposals & Voting\n\n- `createProposal(title, description) : async Result<Proposal, CreateError>` — shared. Requires a registered caller. The caller must hold at least 1 We-Coin; otherwise it returns `#err(#notEnoughWeCoins)`. On success it creates a proposal with zero tallies and `status = #active`, and the caller becomes its `creator`.\n- `getProposals() : async [Proposal]` — query. Public; no caller check. Returns all proposals, each with its `status` (`#active` or `#closed`) and live yes/no tallies.\n- `getProposal(id) : async ?Proposal` — query. Public; no caller check. Returns `null` when no proposal has that id.\n- `getMyVotes() : async [(Nat, Bool)]` — query. Requires a registered caller. Returns the caller's already-cast votes as a list of `(proposalId, inFavor)` pairs, filtered to the caller's principal. An empty list means the caller has not voted on any proposal. This supports the \"a voter who already voted sees their cast vote and cannot vote again\" UX on page load.\n- `voteOnProposal(proposalId, inFavor) : async Result<(), VoteError>` — shared. Requires a registered caller. Deducts exactly 1 We-Coin from the caller's balance (requires a balance of at least 1) and casts a single Yes/No vote. Returns `#err(#proposalNotFound)` when no proposal has that id, `#err(#proposalClosed)` when the proposal is `#closed`, `#err(#alreadyVoted)` when the caller already voted on that proposal, and `#err(#notEnoughWeCoins)` when the caller holds fewer than 1 We-Coin. On success it increments the proposal's yes/no tally, records a `#voted` activity event, and returns `#ok(())`.\n- `closeProposal(proposalId) : async Result<(), CloseError>` — shared. Requires a registered caller. Closes a proposal, locking further voting. Returns `#err(#proposalNotFound)` when no proposal has that id, `#err(#notCreator)` when the caller is not the proposal's creator, and `#err(#alreadyClosed)` when the proposal is already `#closed`. Only the creator may close their own proposal.\n\n### OQL Query Layer\n\n- `schema() : async Text` — query. Returns the JSON schema of the entities the caller may read.\n- `execute(qJson) : async Result` — query. Executes an OQL query. Traps `OQL: invalid query — <detail>` on a malformed query.\n\n### Documentation\n\n- `getApiDoc() : async Text` — query. Public. Returns this document.\n\n## OQL Entities & Authorization\n\nEach persisted collection is exposed as an OQL entity with per-table authorization:\n\n- `user` — per-user economy state. `controllerOrScoped`: the platform controller reads all rows; a signed-in caller reads only their own row (owner column `id`).\n- `workEntry` — work history. `controllerOnly`: only the platform controller reads it; end users do not.\n- `proposal` — governance proposals. `public_`: anyone, including anonymous callers, reads all rows. Each row exposes `status` (`active`/`closed`) and `creator`.\n- `vote` — votes. `controllerOrScoped`: the controller reads all; a signed-in caller reads only their own votes (owner column `voter`). Each row exposes `createdAt` and has no `weight` field.\n- `activity` — activity feed. `controllerOnly`: only the platform controller reads it.\n\n## Units & Encodings\n\n- Timestamps (`createdAt`) are `Int` nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (`Time.now()`).\n- Identifiers (`id`, `proposalId`) are `Nat`.\n- `creator` and `voter` and the `user.id` owner column are `Principal` text.\n- `inFavor` is a `Bool`.\n- `status` (proposal) is a `Text` tag: `active` or `closed`.\n- `kind` (activity) is a `Text` tag: `workEarned`, `staked`, `unstaked`, `voted`.\n- Amounts (`meCoins`, `weCoins`, `stakedMeCoins`, `coinsEarned`, `amount`) are `Nat`.\n\n## Lifecycle & Polling\n\n- Registration is one-time per principal; the first registered caller becomes admin.\n- Proposals are created `#active`; a creator may close their own proposal, which sets it to `#closed` and locks further voting. Voting is only permitted on `#active` proposals.\n- Voting is one vote per user per proposal; each vote deducts exactly 1 We-Coin from the voter's balance.\n- There are no long-running async operations; all methods complete within a single message, so no polling is required.\n\n## Mutation Retry Safety\n\n- `performWork`, `stakeForWeCoins`, `unstakeWeCoins`, and `createProposal` are not idempotent: retrying them repeats the effect (additional Me-Coins, additional stake, or an additional proposal). Callers should not retry blindly.\n- `voteOnProposal` is not idempotent: each successful call deducts 1 We-Coin and casts a vote. A duplicate call on the same proposal returns `#err(#alreadyVoted)` rather than double-spending.\n- `closeProposal` is idempotent in effect: a second call on an already-closed proposal returns `#err(#alreadyClosed)` and changes nothing.\n\n## Errors & Gotchas\n\n- Guarded endpoints trap `User is not registered` for unregistered non-anonymous callers — register first via `_initialize_access_control`.\n- `performWork` requires a description of at least 20 characters.\n- `stakeForWeCoins` / `unstakeWeCoins` trap on insufficient balances.\n- `voteOnProposal` returns `#err(#notEnoughWeCoins)` when the caller holds fewer than 1 We-Coin, `#err(#alreadyVoted)` when the caller already voted on that proposal, `#err(#proposalClosed)` when the proposal is closed, and `#err(#proposalNotFound)` when the proposal does not exist.\n- `closeProposal` returns `#err(#notCreator)` for a non-creator caller and `#err(#alreadyClosed)` for an already-closed proposal.\n- `assignCallerUserRole` is admin-only.\n- OQL `execute` traps on malformed JSON queries."
  };
};
